{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112680","id":3003771792,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6zCeuQ","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112680","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112680.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112680.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112680","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112680/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112680/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112680/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/68335becd4436cb1e956d037fe6bc553589bd973","number":112680,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add support for getting a joypad's battery and connection information","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"- Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/14482\r\n\r\nI decided to split my big SDL3 joypad features PR ( https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107967 ) into several smaller PRs, this PR is one of them.\r\n\r\nThis PR adds the ability to get information about the joypad's battery state (no battery, charging, fully charged), battery percentage, connection state (wired, wireless).\r\n\r\nRelevant SDL documentation:\r\n[SDL_GetJoystickPowerInfo](https://wiki.libsdl.org/SDL3/SDL_GetJoystickPowerInfo)\r\n[SDL_GetJoystickConnectionState](https://wiki.libsdl.org/SDL3/SDL_GetJoystickConnectionState)\r\n\r\nThis PR used to have a name `Add support for querying more joypad information`, but was repurposed to `Add support for getting a joypad's battery and connection information` since getting button/axis names and `has_joy_axis/button()` might not be necessary to be builtin in Godot, and `get_joy_model()`, `get_joy_type()` have been moved into a separate PR ( https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117526 ).\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Old TODO</summary>\r\n\r\n- [ ] `JOY_MODEL_STEAM_DECK` documentation\r\n- ~~Throttle documentation~~ I don't have access to one :(\r\n- ~~`get_joy_num_axes/buttons()`~~ I think checking if a joypad has a particular axis/button is more useful\r\n- [x] `has_joy_axis/button()`\r\n- [x] Mark as experimental\r\n- [x] Supersede https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/89193\r\n- ~~`get_joy_model()` and `get_joy_scheme()` for Android and Web (depends on https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114338 and https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114589 )~~ (Support for other platforms will be done in a separate PR)\r\n- ~~`get_joy_power_state()` and `get_joy_battery_percent()` for Android ( https://stackoverflow.com/questions/78331095/how-to-get-battery-level-of-a-game-controller-from-an-android-application and https://developer.android.com/reference/android/hardware/BatteryState )~~\r\n- ~~`has_joy_axis/button()` for Android and Web based on Godot's mapping system~~\r\n- [x] Mark as available on iOS (see also https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114316 )\r\n- [x] Remove button/axis name functionality\r\n- [x] Remove `get_joy_model()` and `get_joy_type()` functionality since it's been moved into a separate PR ( https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117526 )\r\n</details>","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":890310664,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4OTAzMTA2NjQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:input","name":"topic:input","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_